Recorded audio lives here and is never committed (see .gitignore).

These are working fixtures for manual ASR checks: real speech, recorded by
whoever is developing. Committing them would put a maintainer's voice in a
public repository forever, and they are not needed to build or test anything —
every automated test is model-free and runs from synthetic input.

Record your own with any recorder at 16 kHz mono, or point `ov` at an existing
WAV with `--wav`.
